{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"08b206ecfdb2ff54","type":"text","text":"## Operational Risk\n\nRisk of losses resulting from inadequate or failed people, systems, internal policies, procedures and internal events beyond the companies control.\n\n\n\n### ","x":-280,"y":-190,"width":580,"height":180},
		{"id":"3401d83816e3da98","type":"text","text":"### Managing Systems & Information Security\n\n#### IT Vulnerabilities\n\nSystems failures, unauthorised software downloads by staff, or external hacker attacks can paralyse business operations and severely damage profitability\n\n#### Data Privacy\n\nEnforce data privacy standards to protect confidential client records from unauthorised public exposure.","x":-1200,"y":-10,"width":800,"height":320},
		{"id":"fc267defea27a2be","type":"text","text":"### Managing People (Human Failures & Rogue trading)\n\n#### Occupational Fraud & Rogue Trading\n\nHuman failures range from unintentional errors to occupational fraud (employees abusing their positions for personal gain). A severe risk in financial services is rogue trading where traders intentionally bypass management controls to place unauthorised trades to gain profit potentially causing massive losses (risky).\n\n#### Mitigation Strategies\n\n* **Hiring Precautions**: Performing rigorous background checks, verifying credentials and obtaining character references to avoid recruiting unsuitable personnel.\n* **Aligned Compensation**: Structuring remuneration around risk-adjusted performance using deferred compensation and claw-back provisions (requiring employees to return bonuses if trades later generate losses).","x":-1200,"y":-685,"width":800,"height":450},
		{"id":"26d2ddecc1ae1413","x":400,"y":-640,"width":720,"height":360,"type":"text","text":"### Internal Policies & Segregation of Duties\n\n#### Explicit Governance\n\nBusiness process must map out clear delegations of authority, responsibilities and feedback mechanisms.\n\n#### Segregation of Duties\n\nA fundamental control measure requiring strict operational separation between front-office (trade execution) and back office (accounting/settlement) activities as well as separating cash management from bank account reconciliations to prevent embezzlement."},
		{"id":"4981cdbc599a43c1","x":400,"y":-10,"width":720,"height":450,"type":"text","text":"## Managing Business Environment Risks\n\n#### Political Risk\n\nThe risk that shifts in government alter monetary, fiscal or investment regulations.\n\n#### Legal Risk\n\nThe risk of facing lawsuits from external parties for breach of contract or regulatory violations; managed using in house legal counsel and standardised contract templates.\n\n#### Settlement (Counterparty) Risk\n\nThe risk that a firm delivers money or securities in a transaction, but the counterparty defaults before delivering its side. Mitigated using central counterparties (clearing houses), margin requirements and standardised agreements.\n\n"}
	],
